1. Eliminating Deception and Legal Liability
The 2018 Flaw: Google engineered the system to sound entirely human, omitting any disclosure that the caller was a machine. Recording these calls without informing the other party risked violating wiretapping and privacy statutes in all-party consent states.

The Modern Fix: Today's automated systems mandate upfront legal compliance. A modern agent immediately announces its nature: "Hi, this is an automated assistant calling to book an appointment. This call is being recorded." If the recipient stays on the line, implied consent is established, satisfying regulatory requirements across all fifty states. The objective has shifted from deception to utility.  
